Z||000000||85 gt fiero||12-05-2001||12:24 PM||||You know the 89 fiero gtp with the 4.3 litre in it, the one they stopped on, i heard that they made 15 of them and all of them were crushed <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> why wouldnt they auction them off to fiero fanactics they could make thousands of dollars off of them because i believe they chrushed the last gtp in may 2001 and that really sucked, they could give me them and no one would see them <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. just my .02<P>------------------<BR>RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES AND SOON TO BE BRIGHT YELLOW||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||12-05-2001||12:41 PM||||Practically, its probably the policy of most if not all of the automakers to destroy any concept work or prototype cars they have if its not wanted anymore.  I think it has to do with not wanting their designs, engineering, and concepts to get in the hands of a competing company.<P>An example:  Although I have no evidence of it, but the 89 Fiero concepts probably had the electronic power steering unit in them that was going to be a mid-year option for 1988.  Since the general is just now getting this technology to market (2002 Saturn VUE) it would make sense not to give it out to outsiders before its introduction.  <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">    <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pyric||12-05-2001||01:07 PM||||They may have not been approved to be street legal in the US yet since they never went into production.  In which case you couldn't get it registered, licensed, insured, and could not drive it.  <P>Wouldn't be much fun if you couldn't drive it.  Suppose you could tell everyone it was a late model 88.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||85 gt fiero||12-05-2001||01:24 PM||||but still you could have used it as a show car or swap the vins tag with an 88. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES AND SOON TO BE BRIGHT YELLOW||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||12-05-2001||01:26 PM||||I work at an automotive testing facility.  We either crush all of our prototype parts or send them all off to be crushed.  The worry is not that the designs will be copied.  The reason the company doesn't release prototype stuff is because it is a liability issue.  None of the prototype stuff is tested fully and doesn't have any warranty information; if it got to Joe Blow in the public, if something goes wrong with it then the company is held liable because they built it.<P>Yes, they could sell the prototype stuff for a lot of money, but could be sued for that much many times over if something happened.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
